orow(36, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL WRITE THEM" (6:9) — ON STONES? "WRITE" HERE AND "WRITE" THERE (27:8): THERE ON STONES, SO HERE! OR "WRITE" THERE (Numbers 5:23): ON A SCROLL WITH INK! I LEARN A CUSTOM FOR THE GENERATIONS FROM A CUSTOM FOR THE GENERATIONS, NOT FROM WHAT IS ONLY FOR THE HOUR — THE DOORPOST ON A SCROLL WITH INK (Jeremiah 36:18 the hint). The row on 6:9 ({SP_(36, 2, "על", "גבי", "אבנים")} "on stones"; {SP_(36, 2, "מנהג", "לדורות")} "a custom for the generations"; {SP_(36, 2, "אלא", "לשעה")} "only for the hour"): THE STONES\' WRITING (27:3, 27:8) GRADED AN ACT FOR THE HOUR, not a law for the generations — the two verbal analogies (I2) weighed and the one-time one refused as a source; the compile\'s marker: chapter 27\'s writing is an EVENT on the tape, no daemon. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 6, deu_06_vaetchanan).')
